@node Intro "Introduction"
@{b}XGWorks Lite@{ub} plays Standard MIDI Files (.mid, .kar, format 0 and 1)
and XGworks songs (.XWS) on a MIDI sound module - Yamaha XG, Roland GS or
General MIDI - connected to the Amiga through a serial MIDI interface or
CAMD. It is the little sibling of XGWorks NextGen for Windows / macOS /
Linux / web and reads songs the same way.

It needs AmigaOS 3.0 or newer and a 68020 or better. MUI is used when it is
installed; otherwise the classic window (GadTools) needs nothing extra.
@endnode

@node Start "Starting"
From Workbench: double click XGWorksLite. Tool types:

  FOLDER=<folder>   the folder of the songs
  CLASSIC           the classic window even when MUI is installed

From the Shell:

  XGWorksLite [FOLDER] [CLASSIC]

Without a folder the last one is used, else the Songs folder next to the
program.
@endnode

@node Main_Window "The main window"
The list shows the songs of the folder. A double click or @{b}Play@{ub} plays
the selected song, @{b}Stop@{ub} stops it, @{b}|<@{ub} and @{b}>|@{ub} go to the
previous / next song. At the end of a song the next one starts.

  @{b}Open...@{ub}     a song from any folder (its folder is shown then)
  @{b}Folder...@{ub}   another folder of songs
  @{b}Mixer...@{ub}    the @{"mixer" link Mixer}
  @{b}XGM...@{ub}      the @{"XGM part editor" link XGM}: sounds by name, XG part parameters
  @{b}Lyr.Edit...@{ub} the @{"Lyrics editor" link LyrEdit}, line by line
  @{b}Staff...@{ub}    the @{"notation" link Staff} of a track
  @{b}Jobs...@{ub}     the @{"Job menu" link Jobs} of XGworks (and Demix)
  @{b}Lyrics...@{ub}   the @{"karaoke window" link Lyrics}
  @{b}Tracks...@{ub}   the @{"tracks of the song" link Tracks} and their @{"events" link Events}
  @{b}Roll...@{ub}     the @{"Piano Roll" link Roll} of the track selected in Tracks
  @{b}Drums...@{ub}    the @{"Drum editor" link Drums}
  @{b}Texts...@{ub}    the @{"lyrics and chord tools" link Texts}

  @{b}Position@{ub}    drag to move in the song; what the song sets before that
              point (sounds, levels, effects) is sent first
  @{b}Tempo@{ub}       25 - 400 %, also while playing
  @{b}Transpose@{ub}   -12 .. +12 half-tones, all channels but the drums (10)
  @{b}Reset@{ub}       Song's own / XG / GM / GS: a System On before the song
  @{b}Output@{ub}      serial.device or CAMD, see @{"MIDI output" link Output}

Keys in the classic window: P or Space play, S stop, Help this guide, Esc quit.
@endnode

@node Mixer "The mixer"
The 16 parts of the song, one row each:

  Sound         the sound name (General MIDI names; "Drums" for drum parts)
  Prog          program 1 - 128
  MSB / LSB     bank select (XG: LSB = variation, MSB 127 = drum kit)
  Volume, Pan, Reverb, Chorus
  M / S         mute / solo

The values are read from the song: what it sets before each part's first
note (control changes, program changes and XG Multi Part messages). A
change is heard at once, also while the song plays, and wins over the
song's own messages from then on.

@{b}Save into the song@{ub} writes the changes into the file the way XGWorks
NextGen does: over the song's own messages where it has them, else as new
messages 100 ms after its reset (and never after the part's first note).
The first save keeps the old file as <name>.bak. An .XWS song is saved as
<name>.mid next to it.

@{b}Undo@{ub} goes back to the song's values.

See also @{"Effects" link Effects}.
@endnode

@node Effects "Effects"
Under the parts the mixer has the song's reverb and chorus: the type and
the return level. Which messages are used depends on the song:

  XG  System Effect (Reverb Type 02 01 00, Chorus Type 02 01 20,
      Return 02 01 0C / 2C)
  GS  Reverb / Chorus Macro (40 01 30 / 38) and Level (40 01 33 / 3A)

A song with a GS reset or GS effect messages is treated as GS, any other as
XG. Changes are heard at once and saved into the song like the mixer's.
@endnode

@node XGM "XGM part editor"
One part (@{b}Part 1-16@{ub}) at a time:

  @{b}Sound@{ub}   the sound now (bank MSB / LSB / program and its name)
  left list    the 128 programs, then SFX and the drum kits: a click sets
               the program's main sound
  right list   its variations (bank MSB / LSB and name), the SFX or the
               drum kits: a click sets that sound
  sliders      the XG part parameters: Note Shift, Variation Send,
               Vibrato Rate / Depth / Delay, Cutoff, Resonance, Attack,
               Decay, Release, Bend Range (0 = the sound's own)
  @{b}Part parameters: default@{ub}   all sliders back to 0

Everything is heard at once, also while playing, and saved into the song
with the mixer's @{b}Save@{ub} (XG Multi Part messages: over the song's own, else
new ones after its reset). The names come from the @{"XG4 voice lists" link XG4}.
@endnode

@node Lyrics "Lyrics and chords"
The karaoke window shows the chord now (highlighted) and the next ones, the
line being sung with the sung part highlighted, and the next line.

Lyrics of XF songs (lyric events; "/" new line, "<" new page) and of .kar
files (text events; "/" and "\" marks) are read. Chords come from the XF
chord events of the song.

Keys:
  + / -   text size (helvetica.font from FONTS:, else the screen font)
  D       the letters: plain (no diacritics, any font), ISO-8859-2 (Czech,
          Polish, ... with a Central European font) or Latin-1
  Esc     close

Song texts in Windows-1250 or UTF-8 are converted.
@endnode

@node Tracks "Tracks"
The tracks of the song: number, name, MIDI channel, number of notes, M
(mute) and S (solo).

  @{b}Name@{ub}, @{b}Ch@{ub}    the name and the channel of the selected track (Return
                 changes it; the channel moves all its channel messages)
  @{b}M@{ub} / @{b}S@{ub}         mute / solo the track (its notes are not played)
  @{b}Events...@{ub}     the @{"Event List" link Events} of the track
  @{b}New@{ub}           a new empty track after the selected one
  @{b}Delete@{ub}        delete the selected track
  @{b}Undo@{ub}          undo the last change (up to 12)
  @{b}Save@{ub}          write the song (the first save keeps <name>.bak)
  @{b}Save as...@{ub}    write it as another file

Every change is heard at once: the song is made again from the edited
tracks (playing stops). The mixer's changes stay.
@endnode

@node Events "Event List"
All events of a track, one per line:

  0012:1:000  1  Note      C3   100   480
  position    ch kind      values

Click a line to select it; it is copied into the edit line below. Change
the line and press Return (or @{b}Apply@{ub}) to replace the event, Shift+Return
(or @{b}Insert@{ub}) to add it as a new event. Del or @{b}Delete@{ub} deletes the selected
event; Cursor up / down (with Shift: a page) moves.

The kinds and their values:

  Note       key (C3 = 60, F#4, or a number), velocity, length in ticks
  NoteOff    key, velocity          PolyPress  key, value
  Ctrl       number, value          Prog       1 - 128
  ChPress    value                  Pitch      -8192 .. 8191
  SysEx      hex bytes, F0 ... F7
  Tempo      BPM (e.g. 120.5)       TimeSig    e.g. 3/4
  Text, Lyric, Marker, Name, Cue, Copyright, Instrument   "text"
             (\r and \n are line / page ends, \xHH a byte the letters
             of the window cannot show)
  Chord      an XF chord: Am7, C/E, Gsus4, N.C.
  Meta       type and hex data

The position is bar:beat:tick (by the song's time signatures); the
channel may be left out (the track's channel is taken).

@{b}Show@{ub} (the cycle gadget) lists only some events: Notes, Controls (controllers,
programs, pressure, pitch bend), Lyrics, Chords, Texts (text, marker, name,
...), SysEx, Tempo (tempo and time signatures). So the lyrics or the chords
of a song are edited one by one here.
@endnode

@node Roll "Piano Roll"
The notes of a track on a grid of time (bars along the top) and keys (the
keyboard on the left); under them the velocities. The window can be sized;
the scrollers are in its borders. It shows the track selected in the Tracks
window, else the first track with notes.

Tools (the first gadget):

  @{b}Select@{ub}  click a note to select it (Shift: add to the selection), drag
          it to move the selection (time by the grid, keys by rows), drag
          its right end to change the length; drag on empty space to select
          the notes in a rectangle
  @{b}Draw@{ub}    click on empty space for a new note (a grid step long), or drag
          to the length you want
  @{b}Erase@{ub}   click a note to delete it

  @{b}Grid@{ub}    1/4 ... 1/32, triplets, or off
  @{b}Ch@{ub}      all channels, or only notes of one (new notes get it)
  @{b}Vel@{ub}     velocity of new notes; changing it sets the selected notes
  @{b}H- H+ V- V+@{ub}  zoom in time and in keys
  @{b}Undo@{ub}    undo the last change

Keys: Del deletes the selection; cursor up / down moves it a half-tone
(Shift: an octave), left / right a grid step; A selects all; C copies the
selection a bar later; + / - zoom; Esc closes. A click on the keyboard plays
the key, and a note is heard when it is clicked or drawn.

While the song plays the line shows the position and the view turns the
pages. Every change is heard at once.
@endnode

@node Drums "Drum editor"
One row per drum - the drums the track uses, or all General MIDI drums
(@{b}Rows@{ub}) - and one column per step of the grid (bar numbers on top, the
first beat of a bar in the fill colour). A click on a step puts a hit there
or takes it away; new hits get the velocity @{b}Vel@{ub} (louder hits are drawn
bigger). A click on a drum's name plays it.

It opens on the track selected in Tracks, else the track with channel 10
notes. @{b}Grid@{ub}: 1/4 ... 1/32 and triplets; @{b}Ch@{ub}: the channel (10 for GM drums);
@{b}- / +@{ub}: the width of the steps; @{b}Undo@{ub}.
@endnode

@node Texts "Texts (lyrics and chords)"
Tools for the lyrics and chords, as in XGWorks NextGen:

  @{b}Text@{ub} / @{b}Onto notes@{ub}   the text is put on the notes from bar @{b}Bar@{ub}, one syllable
        on each note start: words split at spaces, syllables at "-", "/"
        starts a new line, "<" a new page. The old lyrics there are
        replaced. The notes are those of the track selected in Tracks (else
        the lyrics track, else the first track with notes).
  @{b}Text file...@{ub}   the same from a text file (Windows-1250 or UTF-8): a line
        end is a new line, an empty line a new page
  @{b}Chords@{ub} / @{b}Onto bars@{ub}  chords such as "C G Am7 F/A" one on each bar, half bar
        or beat from bar @{b}Bar@{ub} ("-" or "." keeps a step empty); the chords
        there are replaced
  @{b}Chords -1 / +1@{ub}   every chord a half-tone down / up
  @{b}Export... / Import...@{ub}   the Midimusic Chord and Lyrics Protocol text
        (Lyr / Chd lines with bar:beat:tick); @{b}Replace@{ub}: an import removes the
        old lyrics / chords first
  @{b}No diacritics@{ub}   lyrics and texts with plain letters only
  @{b}Undo@{ub}

Single syllables and chords are changed in the @{"Event List" link Events} with
Show Lyrics / Chords; the karaoke window (@{"Lyrics" link Lyrics}) shows the result.
@endnode

@node LyrEdit "Lyrics editor"
The song's lyrics line by line (as the karaoke window shows them), with the
bar where each line starts. Click a line: its text comes into the edit line.
Change it and press Return (or @{b}Apply@{ub}):

  - with the same number of syllables they keep their times
  - with more or fewer they go onto the notes of the line (up to the next
    line); the line's start mark and line end stay

Write "-" between the syllables of a word ("Ka-pr se pla-ca"). The
characters - / < themselves are written \- \/ \<, a backslash \\, and a
letter the window's letters cannot show \xHH (as it was).
@endnode

@node Staff "Staff"
The notes of a track as notation, to read (editing is in the Piano Roll
and the Event List): a grand staff - treble clef from C4 up, bass clef
below - with the notes on a grid of sixteenths, open / filled heads, stems,
flags, dots, sharps and ledger lines; bar lines with their numbers.

@{b}Ch@{ub} shows only one channel; @{b}- / +@{ub} the width. While the song plays the line
shows the position and the view turns the pages.
@endnode

@node Jobs "Jobs"
The jobs of XGworks' Job menu, worked the same way as XGWorks NextGen does
(checked against it). Choose the job; its settings appear. @{b}Track@{ub} 0 = all
tracks (the track selected in Tracks is the start value), @{b}From bar / Thru@{ub}
the range, @{b}Notes from / Thru@{ub} the keys (0-127) for the note jobs. @{b}Do it@{ub} runs
the job, @{b}Undo@{ub} takes it back.

  Transpose          semitones; notes leaving 0-127 keep their name an
                     octave lower / higher
  Velocity Modify    Absolute value, or Relative: value x Rate % + Offset
  Gate Time Modify   the same for the lengths (clocks)
  Shift Clock        all events of the range by clocks
  Sort Chord         the notes of a chord low -> high or high -> low
  Separate Chord     the k-th note of each chord k x clocks later (strum)
  Thin Out           of a run of controller / pressure / bend events every
                     second one goes (the first two and the last stay)
  Quantize           grid (1/32 ... 1/4, triplets, mixed), strength,
                     sensitivity, swing with gate / velocity of the swung notes
  Create Measure     bars of a time signature before a bar; the rest moves
  Delete Measure     the bars From - Thru and everything in them go
  Transpose Chord    the XF chords of the range
  Modify Control Data  one kind of data: set or scale its values; a
                     controller can become another one
  Stretch Time       events of the range: from + Offset + (t - from) x %
  Demix by Channel   a track with several channels into one track each
  Demix by Note      the notes of Channels (e.g. 10 or 1-16) into one track
                     per key, named after the drum ("CH 10 - Snare (38)")
@endnode

@node XG4 "Sound names (XG4)"
The sound and drum names of the XGM editor, the mixer and the Drum editor
come from the voice lists of your XGworks V4.0 installation. Copy these
files into the folder @{b}XG4@{ub} next to XGWorksLite:

  Melody.ini, SFX.ini, SFX Kit.ini, Drum Kit.ini

Without them General MIDI names are shown. They are read when the program
starts; nothing of them is built into XGWorks Lite.
@endnode

@node XWS "XGworks songs (.XWS)"
Songs of Yamaha XGworks (.XWS) are listed and played like MIDI files. They
are read the way XGWorks NextGen exports them to MIDI: one track per
XGworks track with all its parts at their places. The .XWS file itself is
never changed; a mixer save writes <name>.mid next to it.
@endnode

@node Output "MIDI output"
@{b}serial.device@{ub}: the Amiga's serial port at 31250 baud (MIDI) for the usual
serial MIDI interfaces. Close other MIDI programs first. Another serial
device and unit can be set in the settings file (device=, unit=).

@{b}CAMD@{ub}: through camd.library (link out.0; unit= chooses out.<n>), for
interfaces with a CAMD driver.

In WinUAE / Amiga Forever: route the emulated serial port to a Windows MIDI
output (IO ports, MIDI).
@endnode

@node XGPlay "XGPlay (Shell)"
The player without a window:

  XGPlay FILE/A,RESET/K,DEVICE/K,UNIT/K/N,DUMP/S,QUIET/S

  RESET    XG, GM or GS: a System On before the song
  DEVICE   the serial device (default serial.device), or CAMD
  UNIT     its unit (default 0; CAMD: out.<UNIT>)
  DUMP     print the MIDI messages with their times instead of playing
  QUIET    no time display

Ctrl+C stops.
@endnode

@node Settings "Settings"
Kept in ENVARC:XGWorksLite.prefs (and ENV:): the folder, reset, output,
device, unit, tempo, the letters and the size of the lyrics.
@endnode
